  "_key": "!scenes!2749f185b382f009",
  "description": "<p><strong>Where Euphoria is held.</strong> A cheap rented flat supplied by Ludivenko — dehydrated food in the cupboards, women's clothing still in plastic wrap in the dresser and closet.</p><p>Only 24 m², and that is correct: the book says the units are packed with people and crowded with extra beds. Play it cramped.</p><p>Details that matter if the runners search: one chair will break if sat on, the refrigerator's freezer does not work, the sink's water filters are foul, and the hot water faucet does not work.</p><p>If the runners annoy the manager it costs about <strong>100¥</strong> to calm him down.</p><p><strong>Rooms:</strong> —</p><p><em>Layout derived from the printed floorplan on Queen Euphoria p.12. Measured 12 × 7 m by legend square (128 x 129 px — no grid is drawn on this plan) — the map carries a \"□ = 1 metre\" legend, so the scale is the book's, not an estimate.</em></p>"
}
